  "verbalization": "Rimegepant is indicated for Migraine Disorder, and this indication is linked to Migraine With Or Without Aura, Susceptibility To through a series of biologically relevant pathways. The evidence suggests that Rimegepant may exert its therapeutic effect on migraine susceptibility by targeting pathways involved in pain modulation and neuroinflammation, which are also implicated in the pathophysiology of migraine. The presence of multiple indications for Rimegepant—spanning different monoclonal antibodies—indicates a potential role in modulating migraine-related processes, possibly through shared mechanisms of action or distinct pathways. The integration of these indications supports the hypothesis that Rimegepant may contribute to the treatment of migraine susceptibility by influencing key molecular targets involved in the disease process.",
